IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cat-domain`
IMPORT `cat-time`

-- Cat Act 2011 (WA) — PART 1, PRELIMINARY (ss 1-4), with the regulations
-- that complete its definitions: Cat Regulations 2012 regs 4-8, and reg 12,
-- which says how long the s 3(1) "registered" status lasts.
--
-- Source: inputs/cat-act-2011.txt lines 139-200; inputs/cat-regulations-2012.txt
-- lines 64-111 and 148-159.

§ `Part 1 — Preliminary`

§§ `1. Short title`

-- INERT. "This is the Cat Act 2011."
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 1
GIVETH A STRING
`s 1 — short title` MEANS "This is the Cat Act 2011."

§§ `2. Commencement`

-- INERT for this encoding. Every date in s 2 (9 Nov 2011, 1 Nov 2012,
-- 1 Nov 2013) is before 25 September 2025, the first date this encoding
-- answers for (cat-time.l4), so no rule here can reach a provision that is
-- not yet in operation. Carried as data so a reader can check it.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 2(c)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2(c) — the day ss 5, 6, 14(1), 18(1), 22-24, 26-35, 41, 49, 55-60 and 86 came into operation` MEANS
    YMD 2013 11 1

§§ `3. Terms used`

§§§ `approved cat breeder`

-- s 3(1): "approved cat breeder means a person who has an approval to breed
-- cats under section 37". Whether the person holds one is an input.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "approved cat breeder"
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an approved cat breeder` p IF
    p's `holds an approval to breed cats`

§§§ `authorised person`

-- s 3(1): "authorised person means — (a) a police officer; or (ba) a person
-- designated as an authorised officer under the Public Health Act 2016
-- section 24(1) for the purposes of this Act; or (b) a person appointed under
-- the Local Government Act 1995 section 9.10(2) to be an authorised person
-- for the purposes of this Act".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "authorised person"
GIVEN o IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an authorised person` o IF
    CONSIDER o's `authorisation`
    WHEN `a police officer` THEN TRUE                                                                           -- (a)
    WHEN `designated under the Public Health Act 2016 s 24(1) for the purposes of the Cat Act` THEN TRUE         -- (ba)
    WHEN `appointed under the Local Government Act 1995 s 9.10(2) for the purposes of the Cat Act` THEN TRUE     -- (b)
    WHEN `no authorisation under the Cat Act` THEN FALSE

§§§ `cat management facility`

-- s 3(1): "cat management facility means — (a) a facility operated by a local
-- government that is, or may be, used for keeping cats; or (b) a facility for
-- keeping cats that is operated by a person or body prescribed; or (c) a
-- facility for keeping cats that is operated by a person or body approved in
-- writing by a local government".
-- reg 4: the bodies prescribed for (b) are Cat Haven and the RSPCA WA.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 4
GIVEN o IS AN Organisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prescribed as an operator of a facility for keeping cats` o IF
        "(a)" ... o EQUALS `Cat Welfare Society Inc., trading as Cat Haven`
    OR  "(b)" ... o EQUALS `The Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, Western Australia`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "cat management facility"; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 4
GIVEN f IS A Facility
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a cat management facility` f IF
    f's `used, or may be used, for keeping cats`
    AND CONSIDER f's `operator`
        WHEN `operated by a local government`  THEN TRUE                                            -- (a)
        WHEN `operated by an organisation` o    THEN `prescribed as an operator of a facility for keeping cats` o   -- (b)
        WHEN `operated by a person or body approved in writing by a local government` THEN TRUE      -- (c)
        WHEN `operated by another person or body` THEN FALSE

§§§ `microchip`

-- s 3(1): "microchip means an identification device of a prescribed type
-- that — (a) is capable of being implanted in a cat; and (b) is designed to
-- record information in a way that can be electronically retrieved".
-- reg 5(1): the prescribed type complies with both AS 5018 — 2001 and
-- AS 5019 — 2001, "as amended from time to time".
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 5(1)
GIVEN dev IS AN `Implanted device`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `of a prescribed type` dev IF
        "(a) AS 5018" ... dev's `complies with AS 5018-2001`
    AND "(b) AS 5019" ... dev's `complies with AS 5019-2001`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchip"
GIVEN dev IS AN `Implanted device`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a microchip` dev IF
        `of a prescribed type` dev
    ... "(a)" ... dev's `capable of being implanted in a cat`
    AND "(b)" ... dev's `designed to record information that can be electronically retrieved`

§§§ `microchip database company`

-- s 3(1): "microchip database company means — (a) a person or body — (i) that
-- keeps a microchip database; and (ii) that is prescribed as a microchip
-- database company ...". reg 6 lists four bodies ((b) and (e) deleted).
-- Para (b) of the definition, "in relation to a particular cat", is which of
-- them holds that cat's record: an input wherever it matters.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 6
GIVEN o IS AN Organisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prescribed as a microchip database company` o IF
        "(a)"  ... o EQUALS `Central Animal Records (Aust) Pty Ltd`
    ..  "(ba)" ... o EQUALS `Global Microchip Registry Pty Ltd, trading as Global Micro Animal Registry`
    ..  "(c)"  ... o EQUALS `PetBase Pty Ltd, trading as Petsafe`
    OR  "(d)"  ... o EQUALS `Royal Agricultural Society of NSW, trading as Australasian Animal Registry`

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchip database company" (a)
GIVEN o                           IS AN Organisation
      `keeps a microchip database` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a microchip database company` o `keeping a database:` `keeps a microchip database` IF
        "(i)"  ... `keeps a microchip database`
    AND "(ii)" ... `prescribed as a microchip database company` o

§§§ `microchip implanter`

-- s 3(1): "microchip implanter means — (a) a prescribed person; or (b) a
-- person holding the prescribed qualifications for a microchip implanter".
-- reg 7(1): (a) a veterinarian; (b) a veterinary nurse.
-- reg 7(2): (a) one or more of two units of competency AND (b) one or more of
-- ten courses, each "provided by a registered training provider" — taken as
-- true of any unit or course the input lists.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 7(2)(a)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 7(2)(a) units of competency` MEANS
    LIST "ACMMIC401A", "ACMMIC401"

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 7(2)(b)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`reg 7(2)(b) courses` MEANS
    LIST "ACM40412", "LGAREGS404A", "LGA40504", "ACM30210", "ACMSS00001", "ACMSS00007", "ACM30410", "ACM40110", "ACM40210", "ACM40310"

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 7(1)
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prescribed person for a microchip implanter` p IF
        "(a)" ... p's `a veterinarian`
    OR  "(b)" ... p's `a veterinary nurse`

@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 7(2)
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds the prescribed qualifications for a microchip implanter` p IF
        "(a)" ... any (GIVEN u YIELD elem u `reg 7(2)(a) units of competency`) (p's `units of competency completed`)
    AND "(b)" ... any (GIVEN c YIELD elem c `reg 7(2)(b) courses`) (p's `courses completed`)

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchip implanter"
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a microchip implanter` p IF
        "(a)" ... `a prescribed person for a microchip implanter` p
    OR  "(b)" ... `holds the prescribed qualifications for a microchip implanter` p

§§§ `microchipped`

-- s 3(1): "microchipped means implanted with a microchip in a prescribed
-- manner". reg 8: "a microchip is implanted in the prescribed manner if it
-- is implanted by a microchip implanter".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "microchipped"; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 8
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `microchipped` cat IF
    CONSIDER cat's `implanted device`
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST dev  THEN     `a microchip` dev
                        AND "reg 8" ... `a microchip implanter` (dev's `implanted by`)

§§§ `sterilised`

-- s 3(1): "sterilised means made permanently infertile by a surgical procedure".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "sterilised"
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sterilised` cat IF
    CONSIDER cat's `sterilising procedure`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST sp  THEN sp's `made permanently infertile by a surgical procedure`

§§§ `registered — s 3(1), and how long it lasts under reg 12`

-- s 3(1): "registered means registered under section 9". reg 12(2)(a): a
-- registration "has effect from the period specified in the registration
-- certificate until — (i) in the case of registration for one year — the
-- next 31 October, unless cancelled sooner; or (ii) in the case of
-- registration for 3 years — 31 October in the final year of that period,
-- unless cancelled sooner; or (iii) in the case of registration for the life
-- of the cat — the death of the cat, unless cancelled sooner".
--
-- FORK F-03: "the next 31 October" after a registration that takes effect on
-- 31 October itself is read as the following year's.
-- FORK F-04: "the final year of that period" is read in registration years
-- running 1 November - 31 October, so a 3-year registration ends on the
-- third 31 October — two years after a one-year registration from the same
-- day would.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12(2)(a)(i)
GIVEN start IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the next 31 October after` start MEANS
    IF   start LESS THAN YMD (DATE_YEAR start) 10 31
    THEN YMD (DATE_YEAR start) 10 31
    ELSE YMD (DATE_YEAR start PLUS 1) 10 31

-- The last day a registration has effect. NOTHING for a life registration,
-- which runs until the death of the cat.
@ref Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12(2)(a)
GIVEN r IS A Registration
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day of the registration period` r MEANS
    IF   `the law is encoded for` (r's `has effect from`)
    THEN CONSIDER r's `term`
         WHEN `one year`            THEN JUST (`the next 31 October after` (r's `has effect from`))                                 -- (i)
         WHEN `3 years`             THEN JUST (YMD (DATE_YEAR (`the next 31 October after` (r's `has effect from`)) PLUS 2) 10 31)   -- (ii)
         WHEN `the life of the cat` THEN NOTHING                                                                                   -- (iii)
    ELSE REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 25 September 2025"

@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "registered"; Cat Regulations 2012 reg 12(2)(a)
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
      d   IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registered` cat `on` d IF
    `the law is encoded for` d
    AND CONSIDER cat's `registration`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST r  THEN     d AT LEAST r's `has effect from`
                          AND `not past the end of the period` r
                          AND `not cancelled by` r
                          AND `the cat has not died`
    WHERE
        `not past the end of the period` r MEANS
            CONSIDER `the last day of the registration period` r
            WHEN NOTHING     THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST last   THEN d AT MOST last
        `not cancelled by` r MEANS
            CONSIDER r's `cancelled on`
            WHEN NOTHING     THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST c      THEN d LESS THAN c
        `the cat has not died` MEANS
            CONSIDER cat's `date of death`
            WHEN NOTHING     THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST death  THEN d LESS THAN death

-- s 3(1) "registered owner, in relation to a cat, means the person in whose
-- name the cat is registered".
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "registered owner"
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
      d   IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the registered owner of` cat `on` d MEANS
    IF `registered` cat `on` d
    THEN CONSIDER cat's `registration`
         WHEN JUST r  THEN JUST (r's `registered owner`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§§§ `other terms`

-- s 3(1) "public place means any place to which the public has lawful
-- access" — an input (Occasion's `in a public place`).
-- s 3(1) "premises" includes land, buildings and structures, and vehicles —
-- a description of where a power may be exercised; no rule here reads it.
-- s 3(1) "transfer" includes "(a) sell, trade, give away, take consideration
-- for, transfer ownership of and offer for sale; and (b) to reclaim from a
-- cat management facility" — a Transfer record is one of these.
-- s 3(1) "veterinarian" — Veterinary Practice Act 2021 s 3; an input.
-- s 3(2): Local Government Act 1995 definitions apply. The only one this
-- encoding needed, "working day", is not one of them (fork F-01).
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 3(1) "transfer"
GIVETH A STRING
`s 3(1) — transfer includes` MEANS
    "(a) sell, trade, give away, take consideration for, transfer ownership of and offer for sale; and (b) to reclaim from a cat management facility"

§§ `4. Term used: owner`

-- s 4(1): "owner, in relation to a cat, means any of these persons — (a) in
-- the case of a cat that is registered, the registered owner of the cat; or
-- (b) in the case of a cat that is not registered, a person who, or an owner
-- of a business or organisation that, ordinarily keeps and cares for the
-- cat; or (c) if a person referred to in paragraph (b) is a child under 18
-- years of age, that child's parent or guardian."
--
-- FORK F-05: "any of these persons" is read as a list — a child keeper
-- remains an owner under (b) and the parent or guardian is an owner too
-- under (c), not instead.
--
-- s 4(2): for an unregistered but microchipped cat, "a person whose name is
-- recorded as the owner of the cat in a microchip database is to be taken,
-- in the absence of evidence to the contrary, to be a person who ordinarily
-- keeps and cares for the cat." Evidence to the contrary is an input.
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4
GIVEN cat                          IS A Cat
      d                            IS A DATE
      `evidence to the contrary`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the owners of` cat `on` d `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` `evidence to the contrary` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the registered owner of` cat `on` d
    WHEN JUST name THEN LIST name                                                         -- (a)
    WHEN NOTHING   THEN append (append `keepers` `their parents or guardians`) `presumed keeper`   -- (b), (c), (2)
    WHERE
        `current keepings` MEANS filter (GIVEN k YIELD k's `since` AT MOST d) (cat's `keepings`)
        `keepers`          MEANS map (GIVEN k YIELD k's `keeper`'s `name`) `current keepings`
        `their parents or guardians` MEANS
            concat (map (GIVEN k YIELD IF `under` 18 `years of age, if born on` (k's `keeper`'s `date of birth`) `, on` d
                                       THEN k's `keeper`'s `parents or guardians`
                                       ELSE EMPTY)
                        `current keepings`)
        `presumed keeper` MEANS
            IF `microchipped` cat AND NOT `evidence to the contrary`
            THEN CONSIDER cat's `name recorded as owner in a microchip database`
                 WHEN JUST n  THEN LIST n
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            ELSE EMPTY

-- The usual question: is this person an owner of this cat on this day?
@ref Cat Act 2011 s 4
GIVEN cat IS A Cat
      d   IS A DATE
      p   IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an owner of` cat `on` d `:` p IF
    elem (p's `name`) (`the owners of` cat `on` d `, evidence to the contrary of the database record being` FALSE)
